### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@contentType = application/json

### Health check
GET http://localhost:3000/up

### 1. Create a workshop -> id 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "workshop": {
    "title": "Intro to Rails",
    "description": "Hands-on introduction to Rails APIs",
    "topic": "backend"
  }
}

### List workshops (active only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/workshops

### 2. Create a session for workshop 1 with capacity 1, so a second registration will waitlist -> id 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "session": {
    "starts_at": "2026-08-01T10:00:00Z",
    "ends_at": "2026-08-01T12:00:00Z",
    "capacity": 1
  }
}

### List sessions
GET {{baseUrl}}/sessions

### Filter sessions by workshop_id
GET {{baseUrl}}/sessions?workshop_id=1

### Show the session
GET {{baseUrl}}/sessions/1

### Session availability -> 0 held, 0 confirmed, 0 waitlisted, 1 available
GET {{baseUrl}}/sessions/1/availability

### 3. Create attendees
# @name createAttendeeA
POST {{baseUrl}}/attendees
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "attendee": {
    "name": "Alex Attendee",
    "email": "alex@example.com"
  }
}

### @name createAttendeeB
POST {{baseUrl}}/attendees
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "attendee": {
    "name": "Blair Backup",
    "email": "blair@example.com"
  }
}

### List attendees
GET {{baseUrl}}/attendees

### Show an attendee
GET {{baseUrl}}/attendees/1

### 4. Register attendee A for the session -> should be held
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/1/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "attendee": {
    "name": "Alex Attendee",
    "email": "alex@example.com"
  }
}

### 5. Register attendee B for the same session -> seat already taken, should be waitlisted
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/1/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "attendee": {
    "name": "Blair Backup",
    "email": "blair@example.com"
  }
}

### List registrations for the session
GET {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/1/registrations

### Show a single registration
GET {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/1/registrations/1

### 6. Confirm attendee A's held registration -> sets confirmed_at, clears hold_expires_at, enqueues a notification job
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/1/registrations/1/confirm

### Confirming again is idempotent -> same result, no duplicate notification
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/1/registrations/1/confirm

### 7. Cancel attendee A's confirmed registration -> releases the seat and promotes attendee B from waitlisted to held
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/1/registrations/1/cancel

### Cancelling again is idempotent
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/1/registrations/1/cancel

### Attendee B should now be held (promoted) with a fresh 10-minute hold_expires_at
GET {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/1/registrations/2

### Confirm attendee B's promoted registration
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/1/registrations/2/confirm

### 8. Cancel the whole session -> transitions the session to cancelled, bulk-cancels attendee B's confirmed
### registration, returns a summary of registrations cancelled per prior status, and enqueues a notification
### job for every held/confirmed attendee affected
POST {{baseUrl}}/sessions/1/cancel
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "cancellation_reason": "Instructor unavailable"
}

### Cancelling the session again is idempotent -> same status/reason, zero additional registrations cancelled
POST {{baseUrl}}/sessions/1/cancel
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "cancellation_reason": "Instructor unavailable"
}

### Cancelling without a reason is rejected
POST {{baseUrl}}/sessions/1/cancel
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "cancellation_reason": ""
}

### New registrations against the cancelled session are rejected with a consistent conflict response
POST {{baseUrl}}/workshops/1/sessions/1/registrations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "attendee": {
    "name": "Casey Cancelled",
    "email": "casey@example.com"
  }
}
